window.REVIEW_DETAILS["ny_main-192fed3f792f2abe"]={"key":"ny_main-192fed3f792f2abe","group":"ny_main","uid":"192fed3f792f2abe","rank":94,"title":"authored doc wholesale sales emergency access proposal 001","occupation":"sales_managers","archetype":"authored_doc","subbatch":"corpus_main","prompt":"You are a Sales Manager at Candlewick Partners, taking over the correction of the internal sales proposal for Heronbank Consortium before Joaquin Pichler’s executive review on Friday, 20 November 2026. The proposal is for communal access-control units, and the existing version no longer represents the commercial position accurately. You are authorized to correct the review copy, but not to issue a new client offer or commit Candlewick to delivery.\n\nThe 30 September 2026 proposal showed 60 units at £24,000 each, all deploying from April through December 2027, plus a £960,000 optional support allowance. It called the resulting £2.40 million total “account value,” although no call-off had then been signed. As of 18 November, Heronbank has signed only Phase 1: 18 units for January–March 2027. Phase 2 is 22 units for April–September 2027, subject to funding, and Phase 3 is 20 units for October 2027–March 2028, still indicative. The support allowance has not been accepted or allocated to a phase. Jacinta Fournier uses “account value” to mean signed commitment, while Tomas Macaulay uses it for the entire potential opportunity including options.\n\nOne Phase 1 unit is now wanted at the Dundee site by 18 December 2026; it is a pull-forward, not an additional unit. A rarely used emergency-access provision in the England and Wales master schedule permits accelerated shipment on an authorized written instruction while an amended purchase order is pending, without changing quantity or price. No such instruction or amended purchase order has been received. Dundee is in Scotland, the Scotland addendum is unsigned, and Naledi Jankowski has not confirmed that the provision extends there. Heronbank has flagged a possible £250,000 downstream site-delay charge if the handover is missed, but nothing currently shows that charge passing to Candlewick. Ludmila Wickramasinghe has only 90 minutes for delivery validation tomorrow, and Tomas cannot complete the normal finance reconciliation until Monday, so the standard cross-functional approval cannot finish before the review.\n\nCreate `heronbank_corrected_executive_sales_proposal.pptx` as one editable, self-contained presentation of no more than seven slides, including the title slide. It must let legal and contracting stakeholders reconcile the two positions, understand the material changes and distinguish verified facts, disputed assumptions and unresolved matters, while keeping the Dundee exception separate from ordinary account guidance. Do not make a go/no-go recommendation or invent prices, probabilities, dates, approvals or legal conclusions. There are no attachments. Write the file at the top level of the working directory using exactly that filename.\n\n---\n\nWrite your finished work to the **top level of the current working directory**, using exactly these filenames:\n\n- `heronbank_corrected_executive_sales_proposal.pptx` — Editable corrected executive sales proposal for legal and contracting review. (No more than seven slides, including the title slide; Self-contained and editable; Prepared for internal executive, legal and contracting review rather than client issue; Must compare the 30 September 2026 and 18 November 2026 positions; Must distinguish verified facts, disputed assumptions and unresolved matters; Must keep the Dundee emergency case separate from ordinary account guidance; Must not make a go/no-go recommendation or invent unsupported facts)\n\nNothing outside those filenames is collected. A correct file written anywhere else, or under any other name, scores zero.\n","inputs":[],"gold":[{"name":"package/private/gold/heronbank_corrected_executive_sales_proposal.pptx","bytes":50421,"extension":".pptx","url":"assets/a130fb1eb93df72b61aaf7ffdfd2e47a98b75395a03c8dbcbce1ab2e3b29e4e6.pptx","sha256":"a130fb1eb93df72b61aaf7ffdfd2e47a98b75395a03c8dbcbce1ab2e3b29e4e6","preview":{"kind":"text","text":"=== 幻灯片 1 ===\nCORRECTED EXECUTIVE SALES PROPOSAL\nREVIEW COPY - NOT FOR CLIENT ISSUE\nHeronbank Consortium\nCommercial position correction\nCommunal access-control units\nExecutive, legal and contracting review ahead of Joaquin Pichler's Friday, 20 November 2026 review.\nAS OF\n18 NOVEMBER\n2026\nPURPOSE\nReconcile the 30 September proposal with the 18 November position, preserve open approvals, and isolate the Dundee exception from ordinary account guidance.\nInternal factual review - not a client offer and not a commitment to delivery.\n1 / 7\n\n=== 幻灯片 2 ===\n1. VALUE PERIMETER\nName the commercial position before quoting a value\nThe phrase 'account value' is not used as an unqualified headline in this review copy.\nDISPUTED USAGE\nTwo meanings remain in circulation\nJacinta Fournier: signed commitment.  Tomas Macaulay: entire potential opportunity, including options.  Neither meaning is assumed to be agreed.\nSigned commitment\n£432,000\nBasis: Phase 1 only - 18 signed units at £24,000 each.\nSTATUS: SIGNED ONLY\nEquipment pipeline\n£1,440,000\nBasis: all 60 equipment units; 18 signed and 42 unsigned.\nSTATUS: MIXED COMMITMENT\nFull potential\n£2,400,000\nBasis: equipment pipeline £1,440,000 + optional support £960,000.\nSTATUS: POTENTIAL, NOT COMMITMENT\nVERIFIED FACT\nSupport allowance\n£960,000 is optional, unaccepted and unallocated to a phase. It is excluded from signed commitment.\nControl: use the named perimeter and basis shown above; do not substitute 'account value' without a qualifier.\nCANDLEWICK PARTNERS  |  HERONBANK CONSORTIUM  |  INTERNAL REVIEW ONLY  |  AS OF 18 NOVEMBER 2026\n2 / 7\n\n=== 幻灯片 3 ===\n2. CORRECTION OVERVIEW\n30 September baseline vs 18 November review position\nThe prior proposal is retained as a historical baseline; it was not signed business at that date.\n30 SEPTEMBER 2026 - PRIOR PROPOSAL\nHISTORICAL\n60 units at £24,000 each; equipment potential £1,440,000.\nAll deployment shown in April-December 2027.\nNo signed call-off at that date.\n£960,000 optional support allowance; £2,400,000 was called 'account value'.\n18 NOVEMBER 2026 - CORRECTED REVIEW COPY\nCURRENT\nPhase 1: 18 units, Jan-Mar 2027, signed; £432,000 commitment.\nPhase 2: 22 units, Apr-Sep 2027, subject to funding; £528,000 pipeline.\nPhase 3: 20 units, Oct 2027-Mar 2028, indicative; £480,000 pipeline.\nSupport remains optional, unaccepted and unallocated; no new client offer is issued.\nMATERIAL CHANGES EXPLAINED\nStatement changed\nCorrected treatment\nWhy it changed\nCommitment status\nPhase 1 alone is signed; £432,000 is the commitment boundary.\nPhase 1 was executed after 30 September.\nDeployment timing\nThree phases run Jan 2027 through Mar 2028.\nThe account was rephased; the earlier April-Dec 2027 window is superseded.\nDundee unit\nOne of the 18 Phase 1 units is requested for 18 Dec 2026 handover.\nPull-forward only; neither total quantity nor unit price changes.\nValue terminology\nUse signed commitment, equipment pipeline, or full potential.\nThe prior £2.40m label blended equipment potential and an unaccepted option.\nCANDLEWICK PARTNERS  |  HERONBANK CONSORTIUM  |  INTERNAL REVIEW ONLY  |  AS OF 18 NOVEMBER 2026\n3 / 7\n\n=== 幻灯片 4 ===\n3. CURRENT SCHEDULE\nPhased equipment position and commitment boundary\nAll values are calculated at £24,000 per unit. Status labels describe the commercial position, not a delivery authorization.\nPhase\nStatus\nDeployment\nUnits\nValue\nScope note\nPhase 1\nSIGNED\nJan-Mar 2027\n18\n£432,000\nIncludes 1 Dundee pull-forward\nPhase 2\nSUBJECT TO FUNDING\nApr-Sep 2027\n22\n£528,000\nNot signed\nPhase 3\nINDICATIVE\nOct 2027-Mar 2028\n20\n£480,000\nNot signed\nEquipment pipeline\nMIXED STATUS\nJan 2027-Mar 2028\n60\n£1,440,000\nAll equipment; not all signed\nVERIFIED FACT\nCommitment boundary\nOnly Phase 1 is signed: 18 units x £24,000 = £432,000. Later phases are excluded from signed commitment.\nEXCEPTION LINK\nDundee remains within Phase 1\n1 Dundee pull-forward + 17 other Phase 1 units = 18 Phase 1 units. No 19th unit and no 61st unit are created.\nOptional support allowance: £960,000 - optional, unaccepted and unallocated to a phase; excluded from the equipment pipeline and signed commitment.\nCANDLEWICK PARTNERS  |  HERONBANK CONSORTIUM  |  INTERNAL REVIEW ONLY  |  AS OF 18 NOVEMBER 2026\n4 / 7\n\n=== 幻灯片 5 ===\n4. EVIDENCE AND OWNERS\nFacts, disputed assumptions and unresolved confirmations\nLabels are textual as well as color-coded so the evidence state remains visible in print and accessible review copies.\nVERIFIED FACT\nCommercial and schedule facts\nPhase 1 signed; quantities 18 / 22 / 20; £24,000 unit price; stated periods; Dundee and requested 18 Dec 2026 handover; England & Wales wording exists; Scotland addendum is unsigned; no written instruction or amended PO received.\nDISPUTED ASSUMPTION\nMeaning of 'account value'\nJacinta Fournier uses it for signed commitment; Tomas Macaulay uses it for the entire potential opportunity including options. The optional support allowance is unaccepted and its inclusion in a headline opportunity value is not agreed.\nUNRESOLVED\nMatters not yet evidenced\nScottish applicability, authorized written instruction, amended purchase order, delivery feasibility, finance reconciliation, and any evidence that a downstream charge could pass to Candlewick remain open.\nOPEN CONFIRMATIONS AND CLOSURE EVIDENCE\nUnresolved matter\nDecision owner\nEvidence or confirmation needed\nAuthorized written instruction\nContracting authority\nAuthorized written instruction received from Heronbank.\nScottish applicability to Dundee\nLegal counsel - Naledi Jankowski\nConfirmation whether the England & Wales provision applies to the Scottish site.\nAmended purchase order\nContracting authority\nAmended purchase order received.\nFinance reconciliation\nFinance - Tomas Macaulay\nCompleted value reconciliation; normal completion cannot occur until Monday.\nDelivery feasibility\nDelivery leadership - Ludmila Wickramasinghe\nDelivery validation; only 90 minutes are available tomorrow.\nPotential £250,000 charge pass-through\nLegal / contracting\nContractual evidence establishing whether any charge could pass to Candlewick.\nCANDLEWICK PARTNERS  |  HERONBANK CONSORTIUM  |  INTERNAL REVIEW ONLY  |  AS OF 18 NOVEMBER 2026\n5 / 7\n\n=== 幻灯片 6 ===\n5. DUNDEE EXCEPTION\nDundee exception isolated from ordinary account guidance\nThis page describes a bounded factual exception. It is not a general ordering route or a delivery direction.\nDUNDEE EXCEPTION ONLY\nDoes not change quantity or price; does not replace normal approval for any phase; does not create a standing precedent.\nVERIFIED FACT\nWhat changed at Dundee\nOne existing Phase 1 unit is wanted at the Dundee site for 18 Dec 2026 handover.\nIt is a pull-forward from the 18-unit Phase 1 quantity, not an additional unit.\nThe other 17 Phase 1 units remain within the Jan-Mar 2027 phase schedule.\nUNRESOLVED\nContract position - not a legal conclusion\nEngland & Wales master schedule: wording permits accelerated shipment on authorized written instruction while an amended PO is pending.\nThe provision does not change quantity or price.\nDundee is in Scotland; the Scotland addendum is unsigned and Naledi Jankowski has not confirmed applicability there.\nContracting or legal confirmation is needed before the provision is relied upon.\nUNRESOLVED\nEvidence gap and release controls\nNeither authorized written instruction nor amended purchase order has been received.\nCustomer-reported downstream exposure\nHeronbank flagged a possible £250,000 site-delay charge if the handover is missed. No evidence establishes pass-through to Candlewick.\nBefore acceleration is executable\nCandlewick requires: authorized written instruction + contractual applicability confirmation + delivery feasibility.\nBoundary: urgency alone is not authorization. The Dundee exception leaves ordinary phase governance and cross-functional approval unchanged.\nCANDLEWICK PARTNERS  |  HERONBANK CONSORTIUM  |  INTERNAL REVIEW ONLY  |  AS OF 18 NOVEMBER 2026\n6 / 7\n\n=== 幻灯片 7 ===\n6. REVIEW-ONLY HANDLING\nCorrection record, incomplete approvals and review scope\nThis provisional copy enables review of the corrected facts without implying approval by silence, elapsed time or meeting attendance.\nCORRECTION RECORD\nPrior statement\nCorrected treatment\nReason\n£2.40m called 'account value'\nUse named perimeters: £432k signed commitment; £1.44m equipment pipeline; £2.40m full potential.\nPrior label combined equipment potential with optional support.\n60 units Apr-Dec 2027\n18 signed Jan-Mar 2027; 22 subject to funding Apr-Sep 2027; 20 indicative Oct 2027-Mar 2028.\nPhase 1 was signed and deployment was rephased.\nNo signed call-off\nPhase 1 only is signed: 18 units and £432,000.\nCommitment status changed after 30 September.\nNo exception treatment\nDundee is isolated as one Phase 1 pull-forward with evidence gates.\nUrgent request, missing documents, and unconfirmed Scottish applicability.\nREVIEW-ONLY STATUS\nApproval handling remains explicit\nPrepared for executive, legal and contracting review before Joaquin Pichler's Friday, 20 Nov review.\nFinance reconciliation: Tomas Macaulay cannot complete the normal reconciliation until Monday.\nDelivery validation: Ludmila Wickramasinghe has a 90-minute window tomorrow.\nLegal / contracting: Scottish applicability and missing instruction / amended PO remain open.\nNo client-issued offer, approval, or commitment to delivery is created by this review copy.\nReview scope: reconcile commercial perimeters, record the Dundee evidence gaps, and preserve pending finance, legal and delivery confirmation. No go/no-go recommendation is made in this document.\nCANDLEWICK PARTNERS  |  HERONBANK CONSORTIUM  |  INTERNAL REVIEW ONLY  |  AS OF 18 NOVEMBER 2026\n7 / 7","truncated":false,"note":"PPTX 共7页的文字提取；不还原位置、动画和版式。","embedded_image_count":0,"embedded_images":[]}}],"rubric":[{"rubric_item_id":"R01","check":"file_introspection","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The exact required PPTX file exists at the top level of the working directory and opens as a valid presentation.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":true,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Submitted file and its package structure.","grader_hint":"Confirm that `heronbank_corrected_executive_sales_proposal.pptx` exists in the submission root and can be opened or parsed without repair."},{"rubric_item_id":"R02","check":"file_introspection","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The presentation contains no more than seven slides, counting the title slide.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"PPTX slide count.","grader_hint":"Inspect the presentation package or open the deck and count all slides, including hidden slides."},{"rubric_item_id":"R03","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The deck identifies itself as a corrected internal review version, carries an as-of date of 18 November 2026, and does not appear to be a client-issued offer.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Title, subtitle, footer or document-control text.","grader_hint":"Accept equivalent wording such as draft, internal review, provisional or not for client issue, provided the date and controlled status are apparent."},{"rubric_item_id":"R04","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The purpose and audience are immediately apparent as executive, legal and contracting review of a corrected commercial proposal.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Opening content and overall framing.","grader_hint":"A reviewer should not have to infer whether the deck is a sales pitch, a final quotation or an internal correction package."},{"rubric_item_id":"R05","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The 30 September baseline is represented as 60 units at £24,000 each, planned for April–December 2027, with no signed call-off at that date.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Period comparison, prior-position summary or reconciliation.","grader_hint":"Check the quantity, unit price, deployment period and historical commitment status together; the prior position must not be presented as signed business."},{"rubric_item_id":"R06","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The current schedule shows Phase 1 as 18 units for January–March 2027 and signed, Phase 2 as 22 units for April–September 2027 and subject to funding, and Phase 3 as 20 units for October 2027–March 2028 and indicative.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Current phased schedule and status labels.","grader_hint":"All three phases must pair the correct quantity and period with the correct commercial status."},{"rubric_item_id":"R07","check":"value_tolerance","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Each phase value equals its quantity multiplied by £24,000: Phase 1 £432,000, Phase 2 £528,000 and Phase 3 £480,000, each within ±£1.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Phase values and underlying quantities and unit price.","grader_hint":"Recalculate the values. Abbreviated labels such as £432k are acceptable if mathematically exact at the displayed precision."},{"rubric_item_id":"R08","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The signed commitment is limited to Phase 1 and equals £432,000 within ±£1; unsigned later phases are not included in that committed amount.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Valuation summary and commitment-status treatment.","grader_hint":"Check both the amount and its perimeter. A headline that includes Phase 2, Phase 3 or support in committed value fails this item."},{"rubric_item_id":"R09","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The equipment pipeline value equals the sum of all 60 units at £24,000, or £1,440,000 within ±£1, without implying that the full amount is signed.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Opportunity reconciliation or valuation bridge.","grader_hint":"Confirm that 18 + 22 + 20 equals 60 and that the equipment total is status-qualified."},{"rubric_item_id":"R10","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The £2,400,000 full-potential figure is reconciled as £1,440,000 of equipment plus a £960,000 support allowance, and the support component is labelled optional, unaccepted and unallocated.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Value bridge, footnote or assumptions treatment.","grader_hint":"The arithmetic must agree within ±£1, and the support allowance must not be portrayed as contracted revenue."},{"rubric_item_id":"R11","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The deck resolves the ambiguous phrase “account value” by explicitly distinguishing signed commitment, equipment pipeline and full potential including options.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Definitions, valuation labels and executive summary.","grader_hint":"Equivalent terminology is acceptable, but a legal or contracting reader must be able to tell which perimeter any value represents."},{"rubric_item_id":"R12","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Every prominent value is paired with a basis and status label that agrees with the detailed schedule; “account value” is not used elsewhere as an unqualified synonym for conflicting perimeters.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Headlines, charts, tables and footnotes throughout the deck.","grader_hint":"Walk every repeated £432k, £1.44m, £960k and £2.40m figure and confirm that its label remains consistent."},{"rubric_item_id":"R13","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The period comparison explains the material changes rather than merely displaying two snapshots: Phase 1 became signed, deployment was rephased through March 2028, one unit became urgent, and total quantity and unit price did not change.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Change narrative, bridge or comparison annotations.","grader_hint":"Credit concise causal explanations. Do not require a particular chart type."},{"rubric_item_id":"R14","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The Dundee unit is treated as a pull-forward from the 18-unit Phase 1 quantity, not as a nineteenth Phase 1 unit or a sixty-first unit overall.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Schedule, exception note and total quantities.","grader_hint":"Check that the urgent treatment does not increase any equipment total and that the remaining Phase 1 balance is arithmetically compatible with one unit being accelerated."},{"rubric_item_id":"R15","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"Verified facts are visibly distinguishable and include the signed Phase 1 status, stated quantities, stated unit price, stated periods and the location and requested date of the urgent unit.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Fact-status framework, legends or labels.","grader_hint":"The distinction must be operationally clear; colour alone is insufficient if labels or another accessible cue are absent."},{"rubric_item_id":"R16","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"Disputed assumptions are visibly distinguished and include the competing meanings of account value and the treatment of the optional support allowance.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Assumptions or issue treatment.","grader_hint":"The deck should not silently select one stakeholder’s usage as though it were an agreed fact."},{"rubric_item_id":"R17","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"Unresolved matters are visibly distinguished and cover emergency-provision applicability in Scotland, receipt of authorized written instruction, the amended purchase order, completion of finance reconciliation and delivery validation.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Open-item register, status summary or equivalent content.","grader_hint":"Accept consolidated treatment, but each material gap must remain visibly open rather than being filled with an assumption."},{"rubric_item_id":"R18","check":"geometry","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The Dundee emergency case is visually and semantically isolated from ordinary phase guidance so that its exceptional status cannot be mistaken for a general ordering route.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Placement, labelling, boundaries and cross-references.","grader_hint":"Inspect the rendered deck. The exception may share a slide with other content, but it needs an unmistakable boundary and exception label."},{"rubric_item_id":"R19","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The emergency provision is represented narrowly: it concerns acceleration on authorized written instruction while an amended purchase order is pending and does not permit a quantity or price change.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Emergency-case description and control conditions.","grader_hint":"All stated conditions must remain linked to the provision; generic language that implies broad emergency authority is insufficient."},{"rubric_item_id":"R20","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The deck expressly records that neither the authorized written instruction nor the amended purchase order has been received.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Emergency status or open-evidence text.","grader_hint":"Accept equivalent explicit wording. A blank field, question mark or generic ‘pending paperwork’ does not establish both missing items."},{"rubric_item_id":"R21","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The jurisdiction comparison correctly contrasts the England and Wales master schedule, where the wording exists, with the unsigned Scotland addendum and unconfirmed applicability to Dundee.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Jurisdiction comparison or contract-position summary.","grader_hint":"The comparison must cover both named jurisdictions and distinguish existence of wording from applicability to the Scottish order."},{"rubric_item_id":"R22","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The practical consequence of the jurisdiction gap is stated as a need for contracting or legal confirmation before the provision is relied upon, without presenting an unsupported conclusion about Scottish law.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Jurisdiction consequence, control gate or legal-review note.","grader_hint":"Credit disciplined escalation language. Reject a categorical legal conclusion that the clause is valid, invalid or automatically extended."},{"rubric_item_id":"R23","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The risk description links Dundee to the requested 18 December 2026 handover and the possible £250,000 downstream site-delay charge while making clear that pass-through to Candlewick is not established.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Emergency risk statement.","grader_hint":"The amount should be exact within ±£1. It must be framed as potential downstream exposure, not booked loss, expected value or established seller liability."},{"rubric_item_id":"R24","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The operating control for any accelerated release requires an authorized written instruction, confirmation of contractual applicability and delivery feasibility before Candlewick treats the exception as executable.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Release gate, control path or conditions-to-proceed treatment.","grader_hint":"This is a professional-control item. The deck need not prescribe system clicks, but it must prevent urgency alone from functioning as authorization."},{"rubric_item_id":"R25","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The exception is prevented from changing ordinary account governance: it does not increase quantity or price, replace normal approval for other phases, or create an implied standing precedent.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Exception boundaries and ordinary-process treatment.","grader_hint":"Look for explicit boundaries sufficient to stop a reader from reusing the Dundee path for routine orders."},{"rubric_item_id":"R26","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Open matters are assigned to appropriate decision owners: contracting authority for written instruction, legal counsel for Scottish applicability, finance for value reconciliation and delivery leadership for feasibility.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Owner fields, action register or control responsibilities.","grader_hint":"The named people supplied in the brief should be used consistently with their stated roles; equivalent role labels may accompany their names."},{"rubric_item_id":"R27","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"Because ordinary cross-functional approval cannot finish before Friday, the deck uses a defensible review-only fallback: incomplete approvals remain explicit, the version is provisional, and nothing implies approval by silence or elapsed time.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Document status, approval treatment and open controls.","grader_hint":"The fallback should enable review without bypassing the missing finance, legal or delivery checks."},{"rubric_item_id":"R28","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"A concise correction record identifies the material statements changed from the prior proposal, their corrected treatment and the reason for each change.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Change record, correction summary or annotated comparison.","grader_hint":"At minimum, the record should cover valuation terminology, commitment status, phasing and the newly isolated emergency case."},{"rubric_item_id":"R29","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"Each material unresolved matter names the evidence or confirmation needed to close it rather than using an unactionable generic label such as “TBD.”","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Open-item descriptions and closure criteria.","grader_hint":"Examples include the signed instruction, amended purchase order, Scotland confirmation, completed reconciliation and delivery validation; exact phrasing is not required."},{"rubric_item_id":"R30","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Quantities, periods, status labels and monetary values remain internally consistent across summaries, schedules, charts, footnotes and the correction record.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"All repeated commercial data in the presentation.","grader_hint":"Perform a whole-deck cross-check. A correct table does not cure a contradictory headline or chart."},{"rubric_item_id":"R31","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The writing distinguishes contractual wording, commercial assumptions, customer-reported exposure and questions reserved for counsel, avoiding unsupported legal or liability assertions.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Labels, qualifiers and narrative throughout the deck.","grader_hint":"Review especially the Scotland comparison and £250,000 exposure. The deck should be precise without masquerading as a legal opinion."},{"rubric_item_id":"R32","check":"file_introspection","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Material text, tables, labels and diagrams are natively editable rather than delivered mainly as flattened page images.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"PPTX object structure and editability.","grader_hint":"Inspect representative slides. Decorative images are acceptable, but commercial content should be editable in standard presentation software."},{"rubric_item_id":"R33","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The rendered presentation is legible and professionally navigable, with a coherent visual hierarchy, readable type, accessible status cues and no clipped or overlapping content.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Rendered slides.","grader_hint":"Judge at normal presentation scale. Status distinctions should not depend solely on subtle colour differences."},{"rubric_item_id":"R34","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"Legal and contracting reviewers can identify the reconciled commercial position, the exceptional case, the unresolved confirmations and their owners without asking the author to explain the deck.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Presentation as a whole.","grader_hint":"Assess practical usability, not merely presence of isolated facts. The presentation should support a time-constrained executive review."},{"rubric_item_id":"R35","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The presentation over-produces by making a go/no-go commercial recommendation, directing that Dundee be shipped or held, or otherwise converting the factual review into a recommended decision.","weight":-7.0,"polarity":"penalty","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Headlines, conclusion, call to action and speaker-facing language.","grader_hint":"Apply the penalty only for an actual recommendation or directive. Neutral control conditions, open questions and identification of confirmations required for execution are not recommendations."}],"spec":{"professional_context":"Candlewick Partners is correcting a single wholesale engineering proposal for Heronbank Consortium after the commercial schedule, valuation language and contract status diverged. The presentation will be reviewed by executives, legal counsel and contracting stakeholders before the ordinary approval process can be completed.","difficulty_sources":["Reconciling signed, forecast and optional value perimeters without losing numerical consistency","Separating an exceptional emergency path from ordinary account governance","Comparing incomplete contract positions across England and Wales and Scotland without making a legal conclusion","Producing a defensible review-only fallback when normal approval cannot be completed","Keeping material evidence gaps visible under a tight slide budget"],"authoring_plan":{"reference_material":{"files":[],"instruction":"Do not create reference files. All transaction-specific facts and arbitrary values are contained in the solver-visible request."},"gold_factual_model":{"prior_position":"At the earlier date, the opportunity comprised 60 units at £24,000 each for deployment during April–December 2027, no signed call-off, and a £960,000 optional support allowance. The earlier £2.40 million label combined equipment potential and an unaccepted option.","current_position":"The current schedule has three phases: 18 signed units for January–March 2027, 22 units subject to funding for April–September 2027, and 20 indicative units for October 2027–March 2028.","numeric_relationships":["Phase 1 value equals 18 multiplied by £24,000, producing £432,000.","Phase 2 value equals 22 multiplied by £24,000, producing £528,000.","Phase 3 value equals 20 multiplied by £24,000, producing £480,000.","Equipment pipeline equals the three phase values or 60 multiplied by £24,000, producing £1,440,000.","Full potential equals £1,440,000 plus the optional £960,000 support allowance, producing £2,400,000.","Signed commitment contains Phase 1 only.","The urgent unit is included within Phase 1 and therefore does not alter the 18-unit phase total or 60-unit overall total."],"period_change_logic":["The change in signed commitment results from execution of Phase 1 after the earlier date.","The deployment horizon moved from a single April–December 2027 window to phases running from January 2027 through March 2028.","One existing Phase 1 unit acquired an earlier requested date; volume and unit price did not increase.","The optional support amount remained unaccepted and should not migrate into committed value."]},"gold_status_model":{"verified":["Quantities, unit price, stated deployment periods and current phase statuses","The signed status of Phase 1","The Dundee location and requested handover date","The presence and limited wording of the provision in the England and Wales schedule","Absence of the written instruction and amended purchase order","Unsigned status of the Scotland addendum"],"disputed":["Whether account value means signed commitment or total potential including options","Whether the optional support allowance belongs in the headline opportunity value"],"unresolved":["Whether the provision is contractually available for the Scottish site","Whether an authorized written instruction will be issued","Whether an amended purchase order will follow","Whether the accelerated date is operationally feasible","Completion of finance reconciliation","Whether any downstream charge could pass to the seller"]},"professional_controls_expected":["Define value perimeters before using the ambiguous account-value label and preserve those labels everywhere figures recur.","Keep the emergency exception distinct from the routine phase schedule and prevent it from becoming precedent or a substitute for ordinary approval.","Require written authority, contractual-applicability confirmation and delivery validation before treating accelerated release as executable.","Treat the possible delay charge as customer-reported downstream exposure unless evidence establishes seller liability.","Use review-only or provisional document control because the normal finance, legal and delivery approvals cannot be completed by the meeting.","Carry every unresolved matter with an appropriate owner and evidence-based closure condition rather than silently completing the trail.","Record the material corrections so reviewers can understand what changed and why.","Reserve legal conclusions for counsel and present the jurisdiction comparison as contract status and an open applicability question."],"imperfections_to_preserve":["The phrase account value has two stakeholder meanings and must not be normalized without showing the competing perimeters.","The support allowance lacks acceptance and phase allocation.","The Scottish contractual instrument is incomplete.","The emergency instruction and amended purchase order are absent.","Finance and delivery validation cannot be completed before review.","The severe downstream exposure has no established pass-through to the seller."],"overproduction_trap":"A conventional sales proposal often ends by recommending approval or immediate action. The intended artifact must instead present the corrected factual position, controls and unresolved decisions without recommending shipment, rejection or approval.","intended_verdict":"A passing reference solution is an editable presentation within the slide cap that reconciles all figures and periods, labels value perimeters consistently, separates evidence statuses, isolates the Scottish emergency case, preserves approval and release controls, documents corrections and remains neutral on the ultimate commercial decision."},"design_constraints":{"artifact_scope":"mixed_media_bundle","structure":"required_sections"},"reference_files":[],"deliverables":[{"deliverable_id":"corrected_executive_sales_proposal","filename":"heronbank_corrected_executive_sales_proposal.pptx","media_type":"application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.presentationml.presentation","description":"Editable corrected executive sales proposal for legal and contracting review.","required":true,"constraints":["No more than seven slides, including the title slide","Self-contained and editable","Prepared for internal executive, legal and contracting review rather than client issue","Must compare the 30 September 2026 and 18 November 2026 positions","Must distinguish verified facts, disputed assumptions and unresolved matters","Must keep the Dundee emergency case separate from ordinary account guidance","Must not make a go/no-go recommendation or invent unsupported facts"],"rendering_required":true}],"work_activity":"plan_work","work_product":"operating_plan","internet_policy":"forbidden","evidence_policy":"closed_world"},"source_metadata":{"prompt_version":"authored_doc@v4","occupation":"sales_managers","sector":"wholesale_trade","task_archetype":"authored_doc","estimated_professional_hours":6.0,"gold_policy_self_report_not_verified":{"author_type":"hybrid","reviewer_policy":"A domain-expert reviewer should inspect the rendered deck and its editable PPTX structure, independently recalculate all commercial values, trace each repeated label and assess whether the exception controls and provisional approval status reflect competent wholesale sales management.","minimum_reviewers":2,"known_limitations":["No source documents are supplied, so the review is limited to the scenario facts and generally expected sales-proposal controls.","Visual quality, legal-commercial discipline and independent usability require professional judgment.","The presentation must not be treated as a legal opinion on Scottish contract law."],"reference_solution_passed_rubric":true}},"validation":{"label":"成品包存在","detail":"按公开题面存在纳入抽样；不视为内容正确性验收。","formal":false,"release_ready_recorded":true,"checks":[{"check":"package_integrity","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-16T14:57:02+00:00"},{"check":"gold_isolation","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-16T14:57:02+00:00"},{"check":"artifact_format","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-16T14:57:02+00:00"},{"check":"rendering","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-16T14:57:02+00:00"}]},"source_path":"/inspire/hdd2/project/special-project-1/public/ynan/gdpval_data/corpus_main/runs/192fed3f792f2abe","declared_deliverables":["heronbank_corrected_executive_sales_proposal.pptx"]};
